.Dd November 12, 2026
.Dt DEBUG_READ 2
.Os RavenBSD
.Sh NAME
.Nm debug_read
.Nd read raw bytes from the debug console
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Fn debug_read buf len timeout_ns
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
copies up to
.Fa len
raw bytes from the console receiver into
.Fa buf
and returns the number copied, which may be less than
.Fa len .
On x86-64 the console is COM1; each received byte is placed in a 4 KiB ring buffer by the
.Fn received-data-available
interrupt and the call blocks on a wait queue until at least one byte is available.
Bytes are delivered exactly as received: there is no line buffering and no CR/LF translation.
Several threads may call
.Nm
concurrently; the receiver wakes one waiter at a time and every waiter re-checks the ring, so a
byte is handed to exactly one reader and a wakeup cannot be lost.
.Pp
A
.Fa timeout_ns
of zero waits forever; otherwise an elapsed timeout returns 0.
.Fa len
of zero returns 0 without blocking.
.Pp
The receive line is ISA IRQ 4, routed through the IOAPIC with the MADT interrupt-source override
when one exists.  If the IOAPIC is unavailable the kernel polls the UART from the timer tick and
notes the fallback in the boot log.  If the ring overruns, the oldest bytes are dropped and the
kernel reports the accumulated count as
.Ql console: rx dropped N
from the reader path, at most once per second; the interrupt handler never writes to the log.
.Sh RETURN VALUES
The number of bytes copied, or 0 on timeout or when
.Fa len
is zero.  Errors are returned as a negative
.Va errno .
.Sh ERRORS
.Bl -tag -width Er
.It Er EFAULT
.Fa buf
is not writable user memory.
.It Er EINVAL
.Fa len
does not fit the address space.
.It Er ENOSYS
The architecture has no console receive path.
.El
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr debug_write 2
.Sh STANDARDS
RavenBSD ABI v1.
